{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVolumeConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVolumeConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whitehead_volume_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whitehead_volume_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L321-L348","doc":"**The Whitehead Volume Conjecture** (van der Veen's theorem):\n`(2π/N)·log|J_N(W)(e^{2πi/N})| → Vol(Whitehead) = 4G`.\n\nSTATE-AND-QUEUED: proved in van der Veen arXiv:math/0611181.  The\nunconditional in-repo squeeze proof for the `⌊N/2⌋` inner sum is now\n`QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whitehead_vc_innerSum_half` (sorry-free,\ndownstream — it imports the `QOU.Knot.Clausen` machinery that this\nMathlib-only base file cannot).  This abstract `kashaev`-linked form with\nthe `(N-1)/2` placeholder index is carried by the class above; bean\nqou-1gkf tracks porting the downstream ⌊N/2⌋ result to this exact form.\n\n⚠ The previous wording called this \"the one honest `sorry` here\".  It is\nnot a `sorry` — there is no such token in the file.  It is a §3b class\nargument, which is the *stronger* discipline: the assumption is in the\ntype, so every caller inherits it, whereas a `sorry` would let a caller\nforget it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit.limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit.limit","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L319-L319","doc":"The limit holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L317-L317","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.WhiteheadVolumeConjectureLimit","kind":"class","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L316-L319","doc":"**CONJECTURE (OPEN).** The Whitehead Volume Conjecture (van der Veen's theorem). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whitehead_vc_of_saddle_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whitehead_vc_of_saddle_value","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L291-L314","doc":"**Conditional VC (sorry-free).**  IF the scaled log of the saddle TERM\nconverges to `4G`, THEN so does the scaled log of the inner sum — immediate\nfrom the capstone (`inner = (inner − saddle) + saddle`, and the difference\n→ 0).  This isolates the single genuinely-open input (the saddle-value =\n`4G` identification, van der Veen's Clausen/Lobachevsky evaluation) as an\nexplicit hypothesis rather than a `sorry`; discharging that hypothesis via\nthe landed `QOU.Infra.Clausen` machinery closes the Whitehead VC. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.innerSum_saddle_scaledLog_diff_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.innerSum_saddle_scaledLog_diff_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L239-L289","doc":"**Squeeze-reduction capstone** (Mathlib-only).  For any choice of level\n`n(N)` and saddle index `k*(N)`, the scaled log of the inner sum and of the\nsaddle term differ by an amount that VANISHES: bracketed below by `0`\n(the sum dominates one term) and above by `(2π/N)·log N` (the sum is at most\n`(N−n)` copies of the max), which `tendsto_slack_zero` sends to `0`.  Hence\n`(2π/N)·log(whiteheadInnerSum)` and `(2π/N)·log(S_{n,k*})` share every limit\n— the VC limit is reduced to the saddle-TERM value (the Clausen step). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.tendsto_slack_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.tendsto_slack_zero","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L221-L237","doc":"**Slack-vanishing brick.**  `(2π/N)·log N → 0` — the term-count slack in the\nsaddle bound `whiteheadInnerSum_saddle` vanishes under the `(2π/N)` scaling,\nso both envelopes converge to the same saddle value.  (Mathlib\n`Real.tendsto_log_div_atTop`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L204-L219","doc":"**Saddle-packaging brick** (E1 at the saddle).  There is a maximizing index\n`k*` in the summation range whose single term brackets the whole inner sum\nwithin the term-count factor: `S_{n,k*} ≤ Σ_k S_{n,k} ≤ (N−n)·S_{n,k*}`.\nTaking `(2π/N)·log`, the two sides differ by `(2π/N)·log(N−n) → 0`, so the\nvolume limit is governed by the single saddle term `S_{n,k*}` — the exact\nreduction the Clausen max-value analysis then evaluates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_le_card_nsmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_le_card_nsmul","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L190-L202","doc":"**Upper-envelope brick** (upper half of the E1 squeeze).  The inner sum is\nat most the term count `(N − n)` times the largest term, so `log` of the\nsum exceeds `log(max term)` by at most `log(N − n) ≤ log N` — the `± log N`\nslack that vanishes under `(2π/N)·(·)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_le_innerSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_le_innerSum","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L177-L188","doc":"**Lower-envelope brick** (lower half of the E1 log-Σ≈max squeeze).  The\ninner sum dominates any single term `S_{n,k}`, so `log` of the sum is at\nleast `log S_{n,k}` for the saddle index — this is the lower bound that,\nat the saddle `k* ≈ N/4` (Whitehead `x* = k*/N = 1/4`), pushes the growth\nup to the volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum_pos","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L167-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadInnerSum","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L159-L165","doc":"The Whitehead Kashaev magnitude as the inner positive sum\n`Σ_{k=0}^{N-1-n} S_{n,k}` summed with the `(2n+1)` weight — the real,\npositive object the squeeze bounds (the `χ_{N,n}` phase is unimodular and\nonly shifts the argument, not the magnitude analysis).  Placeholder shape\nfor the limit statement below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_log","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L121-L157","doc":"**Log-expansion brick** (the `log(2 sin)` Riemann-sum form, analogue of\nthe figure-eight `E5a`).  On the summation range `k + n ≤ N − 1`,\n`log S_{n,k} = Σ_{j=1}^n [ log 2 + 2·log sin((k+j)π/N) − log sin(jπ/N) ]`.\nThis is what reduces the squeeze to the landed Clausen / `log(2 sin)`\nRiemann-sum-vs-primitive machinery. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_pos","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L109-L119","doc":"**Positive-sum brick.** The van der Veen kernel `whiteheadS N n k` is\nstrictly positive on the summation range `k + n ≤ N − 1` — the positivity\nthat the volume-conjecture squeeze proof rests on (analogue of\n`FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_pos`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_factor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS_factor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L76-L107","doc":"Each factor of `whiteheadS` is strictly positive on the summation range:\nfor `1 ≤ j ≤ n` with `k + n ≤ N − 1`, both `jπ/N` and `(k+j)π/N` lie in\n`(0, π)`, so `sin > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whiteheadS","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L69-L74","doc":"van der Veen's positive-sum kernel for the Whitehead colored Jones\n(arXiv:math/0611181, Lemma 1):\n`S_{n,k} = ∏_{j=1}^{n} 2 sin²((k+j)π/N) / sin(jπ/N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.catalanG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.catalanG","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadVolumeConjecture.lean#L66-L67","doc":"Catalan's constant `G = Σ (-1)ⁿ/(2n+1)²`.  `Vol(Whitehead) = 4G`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}